  "extractionNotes": "Employee since 2017 on childcare leave 2021-10-01..2023-10-01, back at work 2023-10-02 (first on overdue holiday); full time. Z-3 salary only 2023-10 (21 of 22 days, childcare leave on the 1st) and 2023-11, 3600.00 each (2023 minimum wage). Employer pregnancy sick pay (code B) 2024-01-01..2024-02-02; the later ZUS sickness benefit is not in the file. The employer's remark explains the base: the 2023 minimum-wage months uplifted to the 2024 minimum wage, 4242.00 less 13.71% = 3660.42, carried over to maternity; recorded as statedBenefitBase (employer-printed, so the expected base is claimed). Birth date: the leave application says 22 May, the corrected ZAM 23 May; ZUS paid from 23 May, so 2024-05-23 is used. ZUS handwritten note on the account screen: case paid, maternity 2024-05-23..2024-10-09 and parental 2024-10-10..2025-05-20. That gives 223 parental days, one short of 224: the employer granted leave to 2025-05-20 (leave application and Z-3) while the corrected ZAM asks until 2025-05-21; the plan follows the employer-granted leave that ZUS paid. Two ZAMs; the second (received about 19 days after the birth) has the full-leave box ticked, and the leave application to the employer is dated 2024-06-03, so 81.5% applies (not printed). The father signed that he will not use parental leave. Employer marked up to 20 insured. asOf = receipt date of the second ZAM (ZUS note undated)."
